# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.3 / §10 S6: the boundaries that render in the IDLE frame — `composer`, `static`, `transcript`.
# The anchor is the degradation notice itself, never the composer placeholder: `render:composer`'s fallback IS a
# bare `>` with no placeholder for the rest of the session (that is the §13.4 contract), so a scenario that waited
# for `Say hi` would wedge on exactly the pane it is testing. The exit is Ctrl-C twice for the same reason — with
# a degraded composer there is no row to type `/exit` into, and "a second Ctrl-C always ends the process" (§7.8)
# is the rule that has to hold under a fault.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect ui: [a-z]+ (pane failed to render|failed) \(
sleep 0.8
send \x03
sleep 0.4
send \x03
eof
